    "viz_md_1": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Station map: the polar projection options\n\n**What this shows** - Seven research stations and two field camps on a NASA GIBS satellite basemap in the EPSG:3031 polar projection, centred on the South Pole.\n\n**The SPL**\n\n```spl\n| makeresults count=9\n| streamstats count as row\n| eval\n    ... (data rows elided; the full query is in this panel's data source, use Open in Search) ...\n    )\n| eval latitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 1))\n| eval longitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 2))\n| eval description=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 0)\n| eval markerType=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 3)\n| eval tooltip=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 4)\n| eval markerColor=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 5)\n| eval markerSize=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 6)\n| table latitude, longitude, description, tooltip, markerColor, markerSize\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. `makeresults count=9` plus `streamstats count as row` creates one row per record; `case(row=N, ...)` packs each record into one pipe-delimited string (`data`).\n2. `split(data, \"|\")` with `mvindex` unpacks the parts; `tonumber()` turns the coordinates into numbers.\n3. `description`, `tooltip`, `markerColor` and `markerSize` style each marker.\n4. `table` keeps only fields Maps+ reads. The helper `data` is dropped, and so is the computed `markerType` (its values are not valid marker types).\n5. Projection options: `antarcticProj=1` switches the map to the EPSG:3031 polar projection. `antarcticMapTile` is the NASA GIBS tile URL template; the `gibsLayerId`, `gibsTime`, `gibsTileMatrixSet` and `gibsFormat` options fill its placeholders and `gibsLowerCorner` / `gibsUpperCorner` set the tile grid extent (the formatter defaults, -4194304 / 4194304). `mapCenterLat=-90`, `mapCenterLon=0`, `mapCenterZoom=3` with `autoFitAndZoom=0` keep the view on the pole.\n\n**Field formats and rules**\n\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Negative = south. `tonumber()` keeps it numeric rather than text. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Negative = west. Only the first row is checked for the required fields. |\n| `description` | HTML text | Click popup. Inserted as raw HTML, so escape any text that comes from events (static text here). |\n| `tooltip` | HTML text | Hover tooltip, also raw HTML. |\n| `markerColor` | png: a named colour; svg: any CSS colour | This query emits hex colours but no `markerType`, so the default `png` applies, and any other value renders a blank marker. |\n| `markerSize` | `w,h` pixels, e.g. `25,25` | Used by svg, custom and icon markers (the default `png` marker does not use it). |\n\n**Try it**\n\n- Add `| eval markerType=\"svg\"` before `table` and add `markerType` to the table list: the hex colours then apply.\n- Change `gibsTime` (yyyy-mm-dd) or `gibsLayerId` to `VIIRS_NOAA20_CorrectedReflectance_TrueColor` to switch the imagery.\n\n> **Studio note:** The GIBS tile host (`gibs-*.earthdata.nasa.gov`) must be allowed by the page's CSP `img-src`; other hosts need a CSP change by the Splunk admin. The polar projection itself has not been verified in Studio."
      }
    },
    "viz_md_2a": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Ice sites on VIIRS imagery\n\n**What this shows** - Four ice shelf and glacier monitoring sites as markers over VIIRS NOAA-20 imagery, same polar projection.\n\n**The SPL**\n\n```spl\n| makeresults count=4\n| streamstats count as row\n| eval\n    ... (data rows elided; the full query is in this panel's data source, use Open in Search) ...\n    )\n| eval latitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 1))\n| eval longitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 2))\n| eval description=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 0)\n| eval tooltip=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 3)\n| eval markerSize=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 4)\n| table latitude, longitude, description, tooltip, markerSize\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. Same pattern as the station map: one `case()` row per site, unpacked with `split` / `mvindex`.\n2. `latitude` / `longitude` use `tonumber()`; `description` is the popup and `tooltip` the hover text.\n3. `table` keeps just the five Maps+ fields.\n4. Only `gibsLayerId` differs from the station map (`VIIRS_NOAA20_...`); the view is centred on the pole at `mapCenterZoom=3`, `maxZoom=6`.\n\n**Field formats and rules**\n\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Negative = south. `tonumber()` keeps it numeric rather than text. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Negative = west. Only the first row is checked for the required fields. |\n| `description` | HTML text | Click popup. Inserted as raw HTML, so escape any text that comes from events (static text here). |\n| `tooltip` | HTML text | Hover tooltip, also raw HTML. |\n| `markerSize` | `w,h` pixels, e.g. `25,25` | Used by svg, custom and icon markers (the default `png` marker does not use it). |\n\n**Try it**\n\n- Raise `maxZoom` above 6 or lower `mapCenterZoom` to 2 to change how far you can zoom and the starting view.\n- Add `| eval markerType=\"circle\", circleRadius=\"12\"` and list both fields in `table` for circle markers.\n\n> **Studio note:** The GIBS tile host (`gibs-*.earthdata.nasa.gov`) must be allowed by the page's CSP `img-src`; other hosts need a CSP change by the Splunk admin. The polar projection itself has not been verified in Studio."
      }
    },
    "viz_md_2b": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Traverse routes as paths\n\n**What this shows** - Two expedition traverses (alpha and bravo) drawn as paths over the polar basemap, one waypoint per row.\n\n**The SPL**\n\n```spl\n| makeresults count=22\n| streamstats count as row\n| eval\n    ... (data rows elided; the full query is in this panel's data source, use Open in Search) ...\n    )\n| eval id=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 0)\n| eval latitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 1))\n| eval longitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 2))\n| eval _time=strptime(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 3), \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")\n| eval description=id.\" — \".mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 4)\n| eval tooltip=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 4)\n| sort _time\n| table _time, id, latitude, longitude, description, tooltip\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. Each `case()` row holds `id|lat|lon|timestamp|note`; the parts are unpacked into `id`, `latitude`, `longitude` and `_time` (via `strptime`).\n2. `description` and `tooltip` give each waypoint a popup and hover text.\n3. `sort _time` orders the rows. Maps+ never sorts, and every row becomes a path vertex in result order.\n4. Options: `showPathLines=1` turns paths on, `pathIdentifier=id` splits rows into one path per `id`, `pathColorList` supplies the colours, `cluster=0` shows each waypoint.\n5. `pathSplitInterval=120` (seconds) only matters when `pathSplits=1`, which is not set here.\n\n**Field formats and rules**\n\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `_time` | epoch seconds (from `strptime`) | Parsed by Maps+; used by `pathSplits` and playback. Sort by it yourself. |\n| `id` | any text; the field named in `pathIdentifier` | Splits rows into paths. Without `pathIdentifier`, all rows form one path. |\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Every row needs coordinates, because every row is a path vertex. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. |\n| `description` | HTML text | Popup; a path takes it from its first row. |\n| `tooltip` | HTML text | Hover text; a path takes it from its first row. |\n\n**Try it**\n\n- Set `pathColor` per path, e.g. `| eval pathColor=if(id=\"alpha\",\"#FF8C00\",\"#00BFFF\")` and add `pathColor` to `table`.\n- Set `pathSplits=1` in the Format panel: a gap longer than 120 s between rows then breaks the path.\n\n> **Studio note:** The GIBS tile host (`gibs-*.earthdata.nasa.gov`) must be allowed by the page's CSP `img-src`; other hosts need a CSP change by the Splunk admin. The polar projection itself has not been verified in Studio."
      }
    },
    "viz_md_5": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Ocean features\n\n**What this shows** - Five Southern Ocean monitoring sites (buoy, polynyas, fronts) over MODIS Terra imagery, same polar projection.\n\n**The SPL**\n\n```spl\n| makeresults count=5\n| streamstats count as row\n| eval\n    ... (data rows elided; the full query is in this panel's data source, use Open in Search) ...\n    )\n| eval latitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 1))\n| eval longitude=tonumber(mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 2))\n| eval description=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 0)\n| eval tooltip=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 3)\n| eval markerSize=mvindex(split(data, \"|\"), 4)\n| table latitude, longitude, description, tooltip, markerSize\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. One `case()` row per site; `split` / `mvindex` unpack name, coordinates, text and marker size.\n2. `latitude` / `longitude` are numeric; `description` is the popup, `tooltip` the hover text.\n3. `table` limits output to the Maps+ fields.\n4. Imagery comes from `gibsLayerId=MODIS_Terra_CorrectedReflectance_TrueColor`; the view is centred on `-70, 0` at zoom 2 with `autoFitAndZoom=0`.\n\n**Field formats and rules**\n\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Negative = south. `tonumber()` keeps it numeric rather than text. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Negative = west. Only the first row is checked for the required fields. |\n| `description` | HTML text | Click popup. Inserted as raw HTML, so escape any text that comes from events (static text here). |\n| `tooltip` | HTML text | Hover tooltip, also raw HTML. |\n| `markerSize` | `w,h` pixels, e.g. `25,25` | Used by svg, custom and icon markers (the default `png` marker does not use it). |\n\n**Try it**\n\n- Set `mapCenterLat` to `-90` and `mapCenterZoom` to `3` to centre on the pole.\n- Add a `layerGroup` field (for example `\"Polynyas\"`) to group markers into a named layer.\n\n> **Studio note:** The GIBS tile host (`gibs-*.earthdata.nasa.gov`) must be allowed by the page's CSP `img-src`; other hosts need a CSP change by the Splunk admin. The polar projection itself has not been verified in Studio."
      }
    }
  },
